[{:db/id 17592186119926 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-feee3179-e7d1-55ab-bcac-f334cca10495"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-feee3179-e7d1-55ab-bcac-f334cca10495" :question/id #uuid "feee3179-e7d1-55ab-bcac-f334cca10495" :question/math-academy-id "q-156620" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the line with equation $4x=2y$ in ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $L$ contains the zero-vector\n- $L$ is closed under vector addition\n- $L$ is closed under scalar multiplication\n- $L$ is **not** a subspace of ${R}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the following two facts about subspaces: \n\n- A set of vectors in a vector space is a *subspace* if it is closed under vector addition and scalar multiplication.\n\n- If a non-empty set is closed under scalar multiplication, then this set must contain the zero-vector (because $0\\cdot v=0$ for any vector $v$). So, if a set does not contain the zero vector, then this set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nNotice that $L$ contains vectors of the form \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 2x\\end{aligned}],\\,x\\in R.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. The coordinates of the zero-vector satisfy the equation $4x=2y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & =2y \\\\ 4(0) & =2(0) \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Let, for example, $a=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 2a\\end{aligned}]\\in L$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ 2b\\end{aligned}]\\in L.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b & =[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 2a\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ 2b\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a+b \\\\ 2a+2b\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a+b \\\\ 2(a+b)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich satisfies the condition $4x=2y.$ Therefore, $a+b\\in L.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Let, for example, $a=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 2a\\end{aligned}]\\in L$ and $k\\in R.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k\\cdot a & =k\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 2a\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}ka \\\\ k(2a)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}ka \\\\ 2(ka)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich satisfies the condition $4x=2y.$ Therefore, $k\\cdot a\\in L.$\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since statements II and III are true, $L$ must be a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7336d919-b96c-5024-ae89-e9caaf4e41d0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7336d919-b96c-5024-ae89-e9caaf4e41d0" :answer-field/id #uuid "7336d919-b96c-5024-ae89-e9caaf4e41d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5175130c-a0e7-5993-877f-e784135b6082" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a149c6f5-ef3c-51ad-997e-db08bfab777c" "answer-5175130c-a0e7-5993-877f-e784135b6082" "answer-7d69583b-f76a-5611-8cb8-4022da72fc78" "answer-44a4e1dc-a2d7-5163-8db3-bd5e766783de" "answer-99e8273a-2cc4-5606-ade8-2988cc10652d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a149c6f5-ef3c-51ad-997e-db08bfab777c" :answer/id #uuid "a149c6f5-ef3c-51ad-997e-db08bfab777c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5175130c-a0e7-5993-877f-e784135b6082" :answer/id #uuid "5175130c-a0e7-5993-877f-e784135b6082" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d69583b-f76a-5611-8cb8-4022da72fc78" :answer/id #uuid "7d69583b-f76a-5611-8cb8-4022da72fc78" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44a4e1dc-a2d7-5163-8db3-bd5e766783de" :answer/id #uuid "44a4e1dc-a2d7-5163-8db3-bd5e766783de" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99e8273a-2cc4-5606-ade8-2988cc10652d" :answer/id #uuid "99e8273a-2cc4-5606-ade8-2988cc10652d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-9b35dfb4-fca3-545e-9624-8422a0c70703" :activity/id #uuid "9b35dfb4-fca3-545e-9624-8422a0c70703" :activity/title "Subspaces of N-Dimensional Space" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186051046 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-a6b1b4f4-42fd-518f-9611-64b9f9fd951d" "step-647ef6bb-9fcf-5b00-95cb-b3da5691fc0c" "step-1821a5bc-a723-5459-b893-12f5b2f84d53" "step-1436249c-5de8-51a2-9062-17b0c4a22818" "step-f20bfc1c-6733-50b5-9d02-7dbeed933bee"] :activity/first-step "step-a6b1b4f4-42fd-518f-9611-64b9f9fd951d" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-a6b1b4f4-42fd-518f-9611-64b9f9fd951d" :step/id #uuid "a6b1b4f4-42fd-518f-9611-64b9f9fd951d" :step/content "question-feee3179-e7d1-55ab-bcac-f334cca10495" :step/next "step-647ef6bb-9fcf-5b00-95cb-b3da5691fc0c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-647ef6bb-9fcf-5b00-95cb-b3da5691fc0c" :step/id #uuid "647ef6bb-9fcf-5b00-95cb-b3da5691fc0c" :step/content 17592186120152 :step/next "step-1821a5bc-a723-5459-b893-12f5b2f84d53" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1821a5bc-a723-5459-b893-12f5b2f84d53" :step/id #uuid "1821a5bc-a723-5459-b893-12f5b2f84d53" :step/content 17592186275391 :step/next "step-1436249c-5de8-51a2-9062-17b0c4a22818" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-1436249c-5de8-51a2-9062-17b0c4a22818" :step/id #uuid "1436249c-5de8-51a2-9062-17b0c4a22818" :step/content 17592186275393 :step/next "step-f20bfc1c-6733-50b5-9d02-7dbeed933bee" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f20bfc1c-6733-50b5-9d02-7dbeed933bee" :step/id #uuid "f20bfc1c-6733-50b5-9d02-7dbeed933bee" :step/content 17592186275399 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
